body:
Slice 3 of 7 of #636. Depends on #655. First store-I/O slice.

## What

- the serialized fleet admission counter, with the CAS-contention retry separated from the upload-id-collision retry — a real bound and jittered backoff. Carried forward from #508's rejected attempts (do not re-earn): a shared 4-attempt budget made `CreateMultipartUpload` answer a false `503 SlowDown` on an empty store at ordinary client concurrency (measured: 8 concurrent -> 2 refused, 10 -> 3, 16 -> 3; aws-cli's default `max_concurrent_requests` is 10);
- Create and Abort semantics per the decision-3 table (idempotent second Abort, no 409 race);
- Abort tears the fence only: the `mpuctl.count` decrement belongs exclusively to the terminal delete (slice 6), and a `Completed` tombstone stays counted — the corrected leg E; the withdrawn "`Completed` releases its admission slot" criterion is unsatisfiable by a conforming implementation and must not be re-earned.

## Acceptance

- 8, 10 and 16 concurrent creates on an empty store all succeed (pairwise-distinct ids, N `mpu:` records, `mpuctl.count == N` exactly — asserted at all three concurrencies, not one);
- Abort per table; `mpuctl.count` unchanged by Abort's fence teardown;
- `cargo xtask ci` green.

Part of #636 / #508 / epic #513.
